before:
Alongside Main.java create study/Labels.java with the code below. Compile with javac --release 25 -d classes Main.java study/Labels.java, then run java -cp classes Main. The class path points to the root above study, not to the study folder.
```java
package study;
public class Labels {
  public static String name() { return "review"; }
}
```

Complete local Java example; the app itself does not execute it:
```java
import study.Labels;
public class Main {

  public static void main(String[] args) {
    System.out.println(Labels.name());
  }
}
```

after:
This is one example with two files. Save each labeled part separately, using the filename shown; do not paste both parts into one file.

```java
// File: study/Labels.java
package study;
public class Labels {
  public static String name() { return "review"; }
}

// File: Main.java
import study.Labels;
public class Main {

  public static void main(String[] args) {
    System.out.println(Labels.name());
  }
}
```
